FILE = "oprah-daily-closing.html"
TITLE = "Oprah Daily, once O, The Oprah Magazine, is closing after 26 years"
TAG = "The Wrap"
H1 = "Oprah's magazine is closing after 26 years"
DEK = "Hearst will shut Oprah Daily, the brand that began as O, The Oprah Magazine, at the end of December. Oprah's attention has already moved to her podcast and a live show in Las Vegas."
META = "The Wrap · Global · 20 Nov 2026 · 3 min read"
LEAD = ("img/wr-oprah-daily.jpg", "Oprah Winfrey on the CBS Mornings set", "vivaia_official / Instagram")

BODY = [
("p", "Oprah Daily is closing. Hearst Magazines, which has published it since 2000, told its staff in an internal memo on Wednesday, 18 November 2026, that the brand will shut down at the end of the year. Women’s Wear Daily broke the story after seeing the memo, and USA Today and others confirmed it the next day."),
("p", "In a statement, a Hearst Magazines spokesperson thanked Oprah and her team for “an extraordinary partnership” and the Oprah Daily staff for building a trusted home for inspiration, wellness and personal growth."),
("h2", "What's closing", "From O to ", "Oprah Daily"),
("p", "If the name doesn’t ring a bell, the magazine will. It launched in April 2000 as <em>O, The Oprah Magazine</em>, a joint venture between Hearst and Harpo, Oprah’s own production company. For two decades it was a monthly glossy, and its yearly Favorite Things gift guide was its most popular issue."),
("p", "The monthly print edition ended with the December 2020 issue. In 2021 the brand was relaunched as Oprah Daily, built around the website oprahdaily.com, with a quarterly print magazine. That is what is ending now: the website and the remaining print issues."),
("p", "The timing stands out. This year’s Favorite Things list came out only days before the news."),
("h2", "The staff", "How it was ", "handled"),
("p", "Oprah met the team over Zoom. According to a person familiar with the situation who spoke to USA Today, she gave each affected staffer a $20,000 bonus on top of their Hearst severance."),
("h2", "What's next", "The page turns, ", "the mic stays on"),
("p", "The magazine is closing, but Oprah isn’t stepping back. At 72, she says her focus now is <em>The Oprah Podcast</em>, which she hosts."),
("p", "Her next big project is <em>Oprah Winfrey’s AHA</em>, a two-hour live show at the Sphere in Las Vegas, for one weekend only, from 2 to 4 April 2027. The idea came to her after watching U2 open the venue in 2023. Grammy winner Jacob Collier will perform, the poet Ocean Vuong will read original work, and Max Richter is the musical director."),
("p", "Put side by side, the two moves tell the story: the woman who built one of America’s best-known magazines is putting her time into a podcast and a live stage instead."),
]

